# ai-doc

Read `docs/ai-doc/INDEX.md` routing only; open **≤3** linked docs. Never read all of `docs/ai-doc/` or `CATALOG.md` unless routing misses. Prefer ai-doc over repo search; verify critical facts in source.

After `storagePool/`, `utilities/`, `cmd/`, or `examples/` changes: update **one** primary page (see INDEX / CATALOG update map). Also `api/endpoints.md` if testserver routes/handlers changed; INDEX/CATALOG only for new topics. No long prose; no duplicate facts across pages.

If any prompt causes implementation changes, update the relevant ai-doc section before finishing. Do not ingest the whole docs tree.
